<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n96412" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στεῖνος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εος</span>, τό, a <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>narrow, close</i>, or <i>confined space</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν ς</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				22.460
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στεῖνος ὁδοῦ κοίλης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					23.419
				</span></i>
			; of the Isthmus of Corinth, <i><span class="en">
				Call.
				<u>Sos.</u>
				 vi 5
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> generally,
				<i>straits, distress</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στείνει ἐν αἰνοτάτῳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					8.476
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μάχης ἐν ς. τῷδε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					15.426
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόνοι καὶ στείνεα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>h.Ap.</u>
					533
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στένος</span> in <i><span class="en">
				A.
			</span></i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σωφρονεῖν ὑπὸ στένει</span> to
			learn wisdom <i>by suffering, Eu.</i><i><span class="en">
				521
			</span></i> (lyr.).</div>
